(D) Materiality Thresholds - A change shall be deemed material - requiring a new referendum - if the
 cumulative total of all modifications since the Baseline meets any of the following:
      • Increases total project acreage by more than 10% from Baseline;
      • Increases projected peak electrical demand by more than 10% from Baseline;
      • Increases projected daily water consumption by more than 10% from Baseline;
      • Changes the primary use or facility type from what was described at referendum;
      • Relocates the primary facility footprint more than 500 feet from the Baseline location; or
      • Transfers ownership or Operational Control to a different ultimate beneficial owner, as defined in
          Section [X].02(J).

